If you are using this as a function (as you appear to be, but your code is
nigh unreadable: if you must use `_' please have some spaces round it) you
want to assign temp to frame 1 *before* calling aov.  It is aov that is
likely to have the scope problem.

My suspicion is that you are not finding the variables in the right place:
try using a clean working directory.

I don't see a new1 or fit.aov1 in your code, for example, so is this output
actually from the code shown? There are several other peculiarities.  You
create P as a matrix but assign to it as a vector: I think you intended P
<- numeric(nrow(x)).  You create a matrix `temp', then mask it by objects
`temp' created in the loop ....

