One point to consider is that with so many observations, the chi-squared
test will be highly sensitive - possibly detecting lack of fit at levels
that are utterly irrelevant to your application.  You might like to try a
test against a subsample of 500 - 1000 (I just made those up; someone may
have a better suggestion) repeated 100 times (for example).

