Have you tried the "For" loop (ie capital "for")?
This might pose a quick fix (clears dynamic memory).
Be careful about the .Audit file getting too big.
Also make sure that your code is as efficient as possible--
no unnecessary storage of big vectors or matrices.
(takes more time but is worth it later)
Another option would
be to write shell script (if working in UNIX)
to call S-PLUS for each iteration
(ie shutting S down after each one and thus clearing the memory).
An even quicker/no memory-worries route would be to
program it up in Fortran or C.

When running big simulations, and other computationally intense
algorithms it's usually optimal to combine S-PLUS with C or Fortran
for speed and to avoid the problems you are having.
One can program the "brute force" work in C, with calls to S-PLUS
to utilize some of the wonderful model fitting algorithms
it offers, for instance.

Good luck

Erin Kammann, ScD
Senior Biostatistician
Alkermes, Inc
Cambridge, MA

