My S+ 2000 procedure of the form

thing <- foo(x, y)

takes about 12 minutes on a Pentium Pro (processor speed not to hand) with
256MB RAM. Since foo() involves calculating the first through fourth
L-moments (using EnvironmentalStats for S+) of 1000 samples each of size
n=100, this strikes me as not unreasonable.

BUT I need to do

thing1 <- foo(x1, y1)
