How are you running this?  Submitting from a script window, or via
source()?

The only ways that avoid this slow-down with a script are to use splus.exe
/BATCH or sqpe.exe: see `S Programming' for fuller details.  But pasting
into the command window is usually also effective.

The background issue is that using source() explicitly or implicitly
via a script window needs to be able to back out the whole task if it
fails, and that's what takes the time/memory.  Don't use them to run
long scripts.

