Message-ID: <84872BFB8F44C94D89DD8F11A163551D178735@grunt.agresearch.co.nz>

Thank-you very much to both Bert Gunter and Renaud Lancelot, who
suggested 3 different ways (all of which work :-) ) of reordering a
factor, thus changing the order that the trellis panels are plotted:

a) DataFrame$Factor <- ordered(DateFrame$Factor, levels=c("Winter Year
1", "Spring Year 1", etc))

b) DataFrame$Factor <- factor(DataFrame$Factor, levels = c("Winter Year
1", "Spring Year 1", etc))

c) Reordering according to some numeric summary of another (numeric)
variable (called Order in the below example): 

DataFrame$Factor <- reorder.factor(Factor = DataFrame$Factor, X =
DataFrame$Order)

Note that in the latter case, Factor MUST be a factor: if you have a
character variable, you will have to coerce it to factor first.

Also particular thanks for determining the real source of my trouble,
which was that I wasn't telling S+ the Data Frame name for the factor on
BOTH the LHS and RHS of the above statements - which is why I couldn't
get the order function to work initially...

Zaneta

