I replied privately, but as the "solution" below made it to the list, I
think it's important to publicly note that  a better approach is NOT to use
apply() at all. SImple subscripting will so it as in dat[,c(1,3)]+
dat[,c(2,4)] . With many columns, the seq() function can be used instead of
c(). Variants of this can be used with functions other than '+' . The point
is, AVOID the use of apply family functions, which are really glorified
for() loops, if possible by using subscripting. Results can be orders of
magnitude faster.

