I think the two of you are speaking (writing?) at cross purposes.

 log x -> -Inf as x -> 0 whereas x log x -> 0 as x -> 0.

Back to the original question, I believe S is doing the correct thing by
reporting 0 * log(0) as NA.  Limits of x*y where x -> 0 and y -> Inf could
take different values.  Its zero in the x log x case, 1 when y = 1/x, and
Inf when y = 1/x^2.  To get around the NA case for x log x I would write a
new function which returned 0 when input 0.

