To be clear, Gunter's code and my code accomplish two different things.  

I (mis?)read Bliese's question as
        'How can I apply a function to the contents of two ajacent columns
as a single _unit_?'
and provided example code showing how this could be accomplished using
standard S idioms.

Gunter, and later James Holtmann, appear to have (correctly?) read the
question as
        'How can I apply a function to the adjacent _elements_ of 2 adjacent
columns?'
They each provide code to answer this question.

Since we read the question differently, our responses also differ.  

As to whether one should avoid '*apply' functions in general, I think that
largely depends on the problem at hand.  With small datasets, it is often
much faster to use a simple to understand and implement method than to find
the fastest one. For large problems, it can be worth finding a more
efficient method.

-Greg

