According to the Splus programmer's guide**, lapply is more efficient than 
a for loop (and apply calls lapply to do it's work).  (Because lapply does 
special things with memory compared to for).  This is my experience in 
practice as well -- I could do many things by using lapply that I couldn't 
do with for loops because of time or memory consumption of the for loop.

[This is of course not to say that there are no faster ways of doing some 
computations than using lapply.]

**(In Chapter 22, "Simulations with S+", "The advantages of lapply", Splus 
Programmers Guides Splus6 for Windows)

-- Tony Plate

