Neither sqrt nor means enter the 
calculation of the uncertainty coefficient U. See Theil, H. 1972, Statistical 
Decomposition Analysis, and Goodman, L.A. and Kruskal, W.H., 1972, "Measure of 
Association for Cross-Classification I, II, III, and IV", JASA.

 

"There really is no known substitute for a little 
diligence in working through problems and reading some documentation" 

 

This is what I did! And I 
needed help to deal with empty cells as S posted NaN as result. Here is my 
newbie code after I received suggestion to deal with x*log(x) when 
x=0. 

 

TheilsU<-function(P,Pidot,Pdotj){
 row.totals<-apply(mat,1,sum);
 col.totals<-apply(mat,2,sum);
 n<-sum(row.totals);
 Pij<-mat/n;
 Pidot<-row.totals/n;
 Pdotj<-col.totals/n;
 
 U.CgivenR<--sum(Pij*ifelse(Pij>0, 
log(Pij/(Pidot%*%t(Pdotj))),0))/sum(Pdotj*log(Pdotj));
 U.RgivenC<--sum(Pij*ifelse(Pij>0, 
log(Pij/(Pidot%*%t(Pdotj))),0))/sum(Pidot*log(Pidot));
 U  
<--2*sum(Pij*ifelse(Pij>0, 
log(Pij/(Pidot%*%t(Pdotj))),0))/sum(Pij*ifelse(Pij>0,log(Pidot%*%t(Pdotj)),0));
 
 list(U.CgivenR=U.CgivenR,U.RgivenC=U.RgivenC,U=U)
 }
UncertCoeff<-TheilsU(Pij,Pidot,Pdotj)
UncertCoeff;

It works fine.

 

Ray. 

 

 

