I usually just add a large enough power of ten, convert to character then
lop off the leading 1 with substring. 

> substring(as.character(1e10+x),2)

If you want a concatenation operator that does things like SAS "a" | "b",
you can create an infix operator like so:

"%p%" <- function(a,b) paste(a,b,sep="")

and use it thus

"a" %p% "b"

See help(Syntax) to find out the precedence of this operator.

