Subject: Re: apply function to mutliple columns
Message-ID: <49479D58D7C2C947B83A2DD3608AC0D9199AED@se2kexch01.insightful.com>

> AVOID the use of apply family functions, which are really 
> glorified for() loops, if possible by using subscripting.

That's not quite true, in S-PLUS 6 at least.  In S-PLUS 6 for Windows,
the common case of apply() on a matrix is implemented in C++, not S.
It's been carefully coded for speed and especially memory efficiency.
It can be much faster than the equivalent for loop, especially if the
for loop uses a lot of memory.  This benefit will be added to the Unix
version with S-PLUS 6.1.

apply() on arrays of dimension 3 and later uses sapply() internally,
after re-arranging the array -- see the apply() source for details.

