You can either

1) use COMPILE with Watcom's C++ compiler to make a foo.obj or
2) use Visual C++ (or Watcom or ...) to produce a DLL and use dll.load.

I presume that COMPILE gave some output which you are discarding: did a DOS
box flash up?  It would be easier to debug by running that in a commands
window.  I also find it easier to use absolute paths for dyn.load.

