-------------------------------------------------------------------

Look at the help files for mdy(), months(), years(), etc.

-------------------------------------------------------------------

tare a look at timeDate() function and timeCalendar formating.  You need to
spesify in and out format.  Here is an example base on what I've seen in
your example:

MonthFunction<-function(date)
        timeDate(date, in.format="%m/%d/%Y %H:%M:%S %p",
                      format="%02m")
YearFunction<-function(date)
        timeDate(date, in.format="%m/%d/%Y %H:%M:%S %p",
                           format="%Y")
date<-"1/2/1986 0:00:00 AM"
MonthFunction(date)
YearFunction(date)

you fill have format like

in.format="%m/%d/%Y %H:%M:%S %p"

-------------------------------------------------------------------

Hi.  Have you tried substring()?  If you always use the format MM/DD/YYYY
(i.e. temp <- "01/02/1986 0:00:00 AM")
then you can use  

MM <- substring(temp,1,2)
DD <- substring(temp,4,5)
YYYY <- substring(temp,7,10).

In the help language reference page for timeDate() the last example is  
 
## Get today's date in yyyymmdd format
timeDate(date(), in.format="%w %m %d %H:%M:%S %Z %Y",
      format="%Y%02m%02d")

To me it looks like this could be used to do the same by replacing
format="%02m" to just get the month, but I just get NA returned (Splus6.0
Windows NT) and have therefore always used substring().

