Brian Ripley has written software for fitting GLMMs using penalized quasi 
likelihood. It's in the latest version of the MASS library, and is called 
glmmPQL (for S+6 and R). It builds on nlme.

Gordon Smyth has reglm for S, also PQL (by another name), simpler.

Jose Pinheiro has GLME for S in alpha/beta, also PQL and similar in effect
to glmmPQL but more integrated with nlme.

GlmmGibbs by Myles and Clayton uses MCMC, currently R only.

Jim Lindsey has a glmm function for R for a single random intercept only,
using simple numerical integration.

Prof Ripley has heard of (but not seen) other functions, e.g. by Doug 
